// File:    Config/Local.xcconfig.example  (copy to Config/Local.xcconfig, which is git-ignored)
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM       Your *Personal Team* id (10 characters, e.g. ABCDE12345).
//                        Find it: run  make team-id  (after Xcode has created your Apple Development certificate).
//                        NOTE: the "(XXXXXXXXXX)" in the name shown by `security find-identity` is NOT the team id.
// WAYPOINT_DEV_SUFFIX    Short unique lowercase name, letters/digits only. Becomes the bundle id
//                        $(WAYPOINT_BUNDLE_PREFIX).<suffix>  (prefix is set in Base.xcconfig: io.github.sachin-khanal.waypoint). Free Apple IDs cannot share a bundle id,
//                        and each person's phone gets their own build.
//
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_TEAM_ID
WAYPOINT_DEV_SUFFIX = replacewithyourname

// --- Supabase (optional until the backend exists; cloud features stay disabled while these are unset) ---
// Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API: copy "Project URL" and the "anon public" key.
// NEVER paste the service_role key here. Keep the odd "https:/$()/" - plain "https://" would be read as a comment.
// SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
// SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY

// --- Gemini (optional): richer wording for the calm guidance lines (opening briefing, landmarks, far-off countdowns) ---
// PREFER THE SERVER: the `narrate` Edge Function holds the key (docs/DECISIONS.md D-047) and builds with SUPABASE_URL set use it automatically, so leave this UNSET.
// The lines below are a DEVELOPER-ONLY fallback, used only when Supabase is not configured. Without a key the app speaks its plain sentences. Warnings, turns and arrival are NEVER sent to Gemini.
// Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey . It is baked into the app bundle on YOUR phone's build: use a restricted, low-quota key,
// never one you use elsewhere, and do not ship it to a public build (the plan is a Supabase edge function in front of it).
// GEMINI_API_KEY = YOUR-GEMINI-API-KEY
// GEMINI_MODEL = gemini-2.5-flash
